  "applies_to": "Price Disio Display room controllers running sequence DX-100 or DX-101.",
  "summary": "Disio Display is Price's room display/controller. In sequence DX-100 it exposes 66 BACnet MS/TP objects (its outputs are named Output 3 - Analog Heat, Output 1 - Actuator Open, Output 2 - Actuator Close, Output 4 - Binary Heat), plus setpoints, loop settings, occupancy, units and network settings. The object list changes with the sequence loaded.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "v1.6.14 Revision: F Version: 17",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Table for Disio sequence DX-100, pages 3-5 of the Disio Display BACnet Object List (v1.6.14 Revision: F Version: 17).",
    "Sequence DX-101 prints the same objects (only the AV 3 Sequence Number default differs), so it is covered here as an alias.",
    "The list names the outputs by terminal (for example \"Output 1 - Analog Fan\"); which outputs exist depends on the sequence.",
    "Multistate states are printed 0-based (for example 0-Unoccupied, 1-Occupied) and are listed that way.",
    "The document has no description column; descriptions are empty.",
    "The document does not say which equipment each sequence is for; only the output names hint at it."
  ],
